    "==> README.md <==
# my-app

A server-rendered SignalX app — one \`vite build --app\` produces the client and server builds. Scaffolded by \`npm create @sigx\` (ssr + resume + cloudflare + tailwind).

## Getting started

\`\`\`sh
pnpm install
pnpm dev
\`\`\`

## Scripts

- \`pnpm build\` — production build
- \`pnpm preview\` — preview the production build
- \`pnpm deploy\` — deploy

## Project layout

- \`src/App.tsx\` — the root component, rendered on the server and hydrated in the browser
- \`src/entry-server.tsx\` — \`createApp(url)\`, the per-request app factory (no shared state between requests)
- \`src/entry-client.tsx\` — hydrates the server HTML
- \`src/styles.css\` — global styles

## Resumability

The page ships **no JavaScript** except a <1 kB event loader. A click loads only the handler chunk for that event; a write to a signal then loads the component chunk and hydrates that one boundary ("upgrade-on-write").

- \`src/resume/\` — resumable components. Handlers may capture only named signals, props and imports (the transform extracts them into chunks).
- \`*.server.ts\` — server functions (\`serverFn\`), callable from handlers and during SSR; the module never ships to the browser.
- \`src/entry-server.tsx\` — \`refreshComponents\`, the registry for single-flight boundary refresh after a mutation.

Docs: https://sigx.dev/core/docs/resume/

## Styling

Tailwind CSS 4 via \`@tailwindcss/vite\` — no config file needed. \`src/styles.css\` imports Tailwind and defines the starter's component classes with \`@apply\`.

## Deploy (Cloudflare Workers)

\`\`\`sh
pnpm build      # dist/server/entry.cloudflare.js + dist/client
pnpm preview    # wrangler dev — run the built worker locally
pnpm deploy     # wrangler deploy (run \`pnpm exec wrangler login\` once)
\`\`\`

\`wrangler.jsonc\` is yours: add bindings (KV, D1, R2, Durable Objects) there and read them from \`env\` in \`src/entry.cloudflare.ts\`. Day-to-day development uses the Vite dev server (\`pnpm dev\`); \`wrangler dev\` runs the real worker over the production build.

## Learn more

- [SignalX docs](https://sigx.dev)
- [GitHub](https://github.com/signalxjs)
",
