    "==> README.md <==
# my-app

A server-rendered SignalX app — one \`vite build --app\` produces the client and server builds. Scaffolded by \`npm create @sigx\` (ssr + hydrate + deno).

## Getting started

\`\`\`sh
deno install
deno task dev
\`\`\`

## Scripts

- \`deno task build\` — production build
- \`deno task start\` — run the production build
- \`deno task deploy\` — deploy

## Project layout

- \`src/App.tsx\` — the root component, rendered on the server and hydrated in the browser
- \`src/entry-server.tsx\` — \`createApp(url)\`, the per-request app factory (no shared state between requests)
- \`src/entry-client.tsx\` — hydrates the server HTML
- \`src/styles.css\` — global styles

## Deploy (Deno / Deno Deploy)

\`\`\`sh
deno task build
deno run --allow-net --allow-read --allow-env dist/server/entry.deno.js
deno deploy      # Deno Deploy
\`\`\`

The server build is fully bundled with the \`deno\` condition; only \`jsr:\` imports stay external and resolve at runtime. \`deno.json\` carries the same tasks for Deno users; day-to-day development runs on the Vite dev server (\`deno task dev\`).

## Learn more

- [SignalX docs](https://sigx.dev)
- [GitHub](https://github.com/signalxjs)
",
