    "==> README.md <==
# my-app

A server-rendered SignalX app — one \`vite build --app\` produces the client and server builds. Scaffolded by \`npm create @sigx\` (ssr + hydrate + node + daisyui).

## Getting started

\`\`\`sh
pnpm install
pnpm dev
\`\`\`

## Scripts

- \`pnpm build\` — production build
- \`pnpm start\` — run the production build

## Project layout

- \`src/App.tsx\` — the root component, rendered on the server and hydrated in the browser
- \`src/entry-server.tsx\` — \`createApp(url)\`, the per-request app factory (no shared state between requests)
- \`src/entry-client.tsx\` — hydrates the server HTML
- \`src/styles.css\` — global styles

## Styling

Tailwind CSS 4 + daisyUI 5. Themes are declared in \`src/styles.css\` (\`@plugin "daisyui" { themes: … }\`); set \`data-theme\` on \`<html>\` to switch.

\`@sigx/daisyui\` ships ready-made components (\`Button\`, \`Card\`, \`Modal\`, \`ThemeSelector\`, …) — see https://sigx.dev/daisyui/.

## Deploy (Node)

\`pnpm build\` writes \`dist/client\` (static assets) and \`dist/server\` (the externalized server build). Run it with:

\`\`\`sh
NODE_ENV=production node --conditions production server.mjs
\`\`\`

Any host that runs Node works — copy \`dist/\`, \`server.mjs\`, \`package.json\` and install production dependencies. \`PORT\` sets the port (default 3000).

## Learn more

- [SignalX docs](https://sigx.dev)
- [GitHub](https://github.com/signalxjs)
