    "==> README.md <==
# my-app

A server-rendered SignalX app — one \`vite build --app\` produces the client and server builds. Scaffolded by \`npm create @sigx\` (ssr + hydrate + vercel).

## Getting started

\`\`\`sh
pnpm install
pnpm dev
\`\`\`

## Scripts

- \`pnpm build\` — production build
- \`pnpm deploy\` — deploy

## Project layout

- \`src/App.tsx\` — the root component, rendered on the server and hydrated in the browser
- \`src/entry-server.tsx\` — \`createApp(url)\`, the per-request app factory (no shared state between requests)
- \`src/entry-client.tsx\` — hydrates the server HTML
- \`src/styles.css\` — global styles

## Deploy (Vercel)

\`\`\`sh
pnpm build                # writes .vercel/output (Build Output API v3)
pnpm exec vercel link          # once
pnpm deploy               # vercel deploy --prebuilt
\`\`\`

The function runs on the Node runtime; switch to \`vercel({ runtime: 'edge' })\` in \`vite.config.ts\` for the Edge runtime.

Day-to-day development runs on the Vite dev server (\`pnpm dev\`).

## Learn more

- [SignalX docs](https://sigx.dev)
- [GitHub](https://github.com/signalxjs)
